            "notes": "## \ud83d\udd39 Round 1\n\n**\ud83d\uded2 Buy:**\n- [Optimal Overflow](item_9d85ca48-b27a-435a-8ef9-247440e0f97d) \n- [Charged Plating](item_b8ca58e7-6ae2-40ee-8618-fe2f32315295) \n- [Compensator](item_2a354f80-610c-4661-9bdd-8960ae1a60b0) \n- [Weapon Grease](item_961ae72f-434f-406b-a89b-ab8efec806bf) \n\n**\ud83e\udde0 Notes:**\nRound 1 is the only round where you might actually struggle with energy. To build up enough healing momentum, you may need to play slightly more aggressively at the start just to make sure you do go out of energy.\n\nTo maximize your bounty, I can\u2019t stress enough how important it is to use your orbs **for healing**. It can sure be tempting to throw out a damage orb \u2013 especially when the enemy is grouped or you see a chance to secure some poke damage. But the problem is this: suddenly, you or a teammate is low on HP, and you don\u2019t have enough energy \u2013 or healing output \u2013 to deal with it. And if you die, you can\u2019t heal. That means missed uptime, missed bounty, and a loss of momentum you can\u2019t afford early on.",
