            "notes": "## \ud83d\udd39 Round 3\n\n**\ud83d\uded2 Buy:**\n- [Phantasm](item_21ed9c3d-7a54-438f-9188-f21fd7a7dbfb) or [Precarious Potency](item_b1305ee6-3027-4131-8797-dcbeb68e3953)\n- [Amari's Antidote](item_67e0b1c5-3bcb-4ab5-b818-5082e5706124) \n- [Ironclad Exhaust Ports](item_2d085fa5-ace6-4fab-9323-b7a06268bcd0) \n\n**\ud83e\udde0 Notes:**\n\u27a1\ufe0f  [Phantasm](item_21ed9c3d-7a54-438f-9188-f21fd7a7dbfb) is your go-to pick this round. It can save your life \u2013 and if you survive, you keep healing. If you die, you\u2019re out of the game for several seconds. **No healing = no bounty = lost momentum.**\n\n\ud83d\udc8a [Amari's Antidote](item_67e0b1c5-3bcb-4ab5-b818-5082e5706124) is an underrated clutch tool. If a teammate drops low, this can be the difference between a wipe or a turnaround.\n\n\ud83e\uddf1  [Ironclad Exhaust Ports](item_2d085fa5-ace6-4fab-9323-b7a06268bcd0) adds **+5% cooldown reduction** and **+25 overhealth**. You\u2019ll feel both \u2013 especially with how often you're fading and orbing. Grab it if you can.\n\n**\ud83d\udca1 Key takeaway:**  \n**Stay alive = more healing = more bounty.** Survivability is your scaling engine.\n\n**Update**\nIf you are up against a strong healer, like a really good mercy, or another healing moira, it isn't wrong to pick  [Cybervenom](item_210a8582-91ec-4cf3-968a-a443f3a0c505) here. But you should also pick  [Cross-Orbal](item_e567bb63-527f-4c72-8ba1-dc59be1a0dc1).   [Cybervenom](item_210a8582-91ec-4cf3-968a-a443f3a0c505)  only activates when you do damage, so [Cross-Orbal](item_e567bb63-527f-4c72-8ba1-dc59be1a0dc1) if a must if you pick [Cybervenom](item_210a8582-91ec-4cf3-968a-a443f3a0c505), as it allows you to continue to heal you teammates, while also activate the perk of the  [Cybervenom](item_210a8582-91ec-4cf3-968a-a443f3a0c505).",
